sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant FM as FM Adapter
    participant P as preCICE
    participant S as preC-SUMO Adapter

    rect rgb(238, 243, 201)
        Note over FM,S: INITIALIZATION - parallel-explicit coupling
        FM->>P: Register FM 2D and 3D meshes
        FM->>P: Set access bounding box for shared source/sink mesh
        S->>P: Register sampling meshes and source/sink mesh
        FM->>P: writeData(initial FM fields)
        Note over S: Initial outgoing data is disabled
        par FM initialization
            FM->>P: initialize()
        and preC-SUMO initialization
            S->>P: initialize()
        end
        Note over FM,S: Initial FM fields are available after initialization returns
        FM->>P: Read received source/sink mesh and readData(relative time = 0)
        Note over FM: Mesh may be empty or response quantities may be zero
    end

    rect rgb(221, 235, 255)
        loop Each preCICE window from tn to tn+1
            Note over FM,S: Independent work uses data available from the preceding exchange
            par FM progresses through the window
                Note over FM: Use installed forcing during FM timesteps
                FM->>P: getMaxTimeStepSize()
                Note over FM: Accumulate FM user timesteps until the coupling boundary
                FM->>P: isTimeWindowComplete()
                opt Mesh reset permitted
                    FM->>P: resetMesh(fm_flow_cells_3d)
                    FM->>P: setVertices(updated FM3D coordinates)
                end
                FM->>P: writeData(FM fields at tn+1)
            and preC-SUMO prepares one response for the window
                S->>P: windowDt = getMaxTimeStepSize()
                Note over S: No internal dt or subcycling - use the full preCICE window
                S->>P: readData(FM fields, relative time = windowDt)
                Note over S: First window uses initialized FM fields
                Note over S: Later windows use FM fields received by the previous advance()
                S->>S: Create connected source/sink dataset using received FM fields
                Note over S: Excess conversion uses these received FM intake constituents
                S->>P: isTimeWindowComplete()
                opt Mesh reset permitted
                    S->>P: resetMesh(sources_sinks_nodes)
                    S->>P: setMeshVertices(updated source/sink mesh)
                end
                S->>P: writeData(connected source/sink dataset)
            end

            par FM completes the coupling window
                FM->>P: advance(accumulated window duration)
            and preC-SUMO completes the coupling window
                S->>P: advance(windowDt)
            end
            Note over FM,S: Exchange and remeshing synchronization complete when both participants advance
            FM->>P: Refresh received source/sink mesh IDs and readData(relative time = 0)
            Note over FM: Install response for the next FM interval
            Note over S: Newly exchanged FM fields are used in the next iteration
            Note over FM,S: Response just exchanged does not use FM fields arriving in that same exchange
        end
    end
    Note over FM,S: Final-window shutdown checks are omitted from this exchange overview
